---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Aaron Holmes | Business Systems, Technical Implementation and Automation"
  description="Business systems engineering, SaaS implementation, REST API integrations, automation, technical troubleshooting and customer-focused delivery."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Business Systems · Technical Implementation · Integrations</p>
      <h1>I make complicated business systems work.</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        I connect technology to the way people actually work. From custom API
        integrations and production automation to customer onboarding and SaaS
        product improvements, I build, troubleshoot and refine systems that
        solve real operational problems.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-links">
        <a href="#experience">Professional experience</a>
        <a href="#skills">Skills and technologies</a>
        <a href="#contact">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">
        Technical problem-solving informed by years in operations, client consulting
        and customer-facing work.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="projects" class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">Selected work</p>
      <h2>Complex problems. Practical solutions.</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        A few examples of the systems, integrations and products I have helped
        build, support and improve. Client details are summarized to protect
        private information and proprietary workflows.
      </p>
      <div class="project-grid">
        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">SaaS product and customer experience</p>
          <h2>TixWork: From Client Tool to SaaS Platform</h2>
          <p>
            An operations and maintenance application originally developed for
            JK&amp;T Wings evolved into TixWork, a restaurant operations platform
            used across more than 100 locations. Today I support onboarding,
            troubleshooting and customer conversations, and use direct feedback
            and restaurant-operations experience to shape product improvements.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">B2B SaaS · Customer Onboarding · Product Feedback · Support</p>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">Custom API integration</p>
          <h2>Healthcare Eligibility and Verification</h2>
          <p>
            Built a multi-endpoint pVerify REST integration connecting eligibility
            and verification services with CRM workflows. Handled authentication,
            requests, response mapping, patient and payer data normalization,
            exceptions and cross-platform troubleshooting.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">REST APIs · JSON · Authentication · Zapier · Zoho CRM</p>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">Data integrity and business rules</p>
          <h2>Centralized Duplicate Processing</h2>
          <p>
            Redesigned scattered duplicate checks into centralized logic covering
            patient matching, product and stage conditions, supplier and owner
            routing, exceptions and a 30-day window. Audited approximately 300
            recent records to identify and correct inconsistent results.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">Deluge · CRM Automation · Data Reconciliation · Testing</p>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">Cross-system implementation</p>
          <h2>New Healthcare Product-Line Workflows</h2>
          <p>
            Translated complex compression-garment intake requirements into
            coordinated processes across surveys, spreadsheets, CRM,
            product and supplier decisions, documents and orders. Mapped the
            differences between operating locations and resolved rollout issues.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">Zoho CRM · Zoho Flow · Zoho Survey · Google Sheets</p>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">Financial-services automation</p>
          <h2>Securities-Backed Lending Systems</h2>
          <p>
            Developed data and document workflows for financial-services clients,
            connecting borrower and ticker information with market history,
            lending criteria, loan-to-value scenarios, prospect research
            and deal-document generation.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">Data Integration · Business Rules · WordPress · Document Automation</p>
        </article>

        <article class="project-card">
          <p class="project-kicker">Healthcare CRM design and prototyping</p>
          <h2>Ask Your Primary</h2>
          <p>
            Helped design and prototype a pharmacy-focused intake system using
            QR-based forms, structured patient-data mapping and links between
            inbound faxes and CRM records. This consulting work led directly
            to my role at Lincoln Health Supply.
          </p>
          <p class="project-tech">CRM Architecture · Intake Forms · Data Mapping · Fax Integration</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="experience" class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">Experience</p>
      <h2>Technical delivery with an operational perspective.</h2>

      <div class="role-block">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h2>SaaS Implementation, Product and Customer Support</h2>
            <p class="role-company">TixWork</p>
          </div>
          <p class="role-meta">Current · Project-based through Ascend</p>
        </div>
        <p class="role-summary">
          Supporting an evolving multi-location restaurant SaaS platform through
          customer-facing technical work, product input and operational guidance.
        </p>
        <ul class="experience-list">
          <li>Support customer onboarding, troubleshooting, maintenance and product questions.</li>
          <li>Translate feedback and firsthand restaurant management experience into recommendations for functionality, workflows and usability.</li>
          <li>Participate in demonstrations, presentations and customer conversations as the team's restaurant-operations subject-matter expert.</li>
          <li>Contribute to technical support and marketing initiatives as the team refines its customer acquisition approach.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role-block">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h2>Business Systems Automation Engineer</h2>
            <p class="role-company">Lincoln Health Supply</p>
          </div>
          <p class="role-meta">Remote · September 2025 – August 2026</p>
        </div>
        <p class="role-summary">
          Became the primary hands-on technical resource for a largely undocumented
          healthcare automation environment spanning more than 400 CRM workflows,
          around 150 existing custom functions and hundreds of Zapier automations.
          The systems supported intake, eligibility, prescriptions, medical
          records, documentation, orders, fax and customer communications.
        </p>
        <ul class="experience-list">
          <li>Built a custom multi-endpoint pVerify REST API integration for insurance and patient verification, including authentication, data normalization, CRM mapping and error investigation.</li>
          <li>Redesigned duplicate-processing and data reconciliation logic; audited roughly 300 production records following rollout.</li>
          <li>Mapped intake variations across three operating locations, coordinating product, supplier, owner and exception rules across Zoho CRM, Sheets, Survey and Flow.</li>
          <li>Led systems implementation for a compression-garment product line, from intake and CRM workflows through documentation and order processing.</li>
          <li>Diagnosed cross-system failures with execution logs and record tracing, identified costly redundant processing, improved support documentation and trained a colleague in ongoing maintenance.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role-block">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h2>Business Systems and Automation Consultant</h2>
            <p class="role-company">AviKaiDo</p>
          </div>
          <p class="role-meta">Remote · November 2019 – Present · Project-based</p>
        </div>
        <p class="role-summary">
          Built websites, integrations, business workflows and automation for
          financial services, healthcare and digital publishing clients.
          Worked from requirements discovery through implementation, troubleshooting
          and ongoing client support.
        </p>
        <ul class="experience-list">
          <li>Built securities-backed lending websites and data workflows for High West Capital Partners, Global Stock Lenders and International Liquidity Partners.</li>
          <li>Helped design Ask Your Primary's pharmacy intake, CRM mappings and fax-to-record prototype.</li>
          <li>Developed content-ingestion and classification workflows and investigated caching and performance problems for TheRedZone.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role-block">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div>
            <h2>Web Development, CRM and Client Project Coordination</h2>
            <p class="role-company">Ascend Internet Marketing</p>
          </div>
          <p class="role-meta">November 2015 – Present · Project-based</p>
        </div>
        <p class="role-summary">
          Supported digital and custom software engagements through development,
          client discovery, planning, issue tracking, vendor coordination and
          technical problem-solving.
        </p>
        <ul class="experience-list">
          <li>Worked on client projects including Schafer Development, Cure Launcher and JK&amp;T Wings.</li>
          <li>Helped connect business requirements with websites, CRM work and custom application delivery.</li>
          <li>Supported the original JK&amp;T Wings maintenance-tracking application that later evolved into TixWork.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="skills" class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">Skills and technology</p>
      <h2>A practical toolkit across systems, software and operations.</h2>
      <div class="skills-grid">
        <div>
          <h2>Business Systems and Delivery</h2>
          <p>Requirements Discovery · Systems Analysis · Process Mapping · Technical Implementation · SaaS Onboarding · Solution Design · Customer Training · Vendor Coordination</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Automation and Integrations</h2>
          <p>REST APIs · Webhooks · JSON · API Authentication · Data Mapping · Workflow Automation · Orchestration · Deluge · Custom Functions</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Programming and Cloud</h2>
          <p>Python · JavaScript · TypeScript · SQL · Node.js · Git and GitHub · AWS EC2, S3, RDS, IAM and VPC Networking · Linux and WSL</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Platforms and Services</h2>
          <p>Zoho CRM and Zoho One · Zoho Flow · Zapier · pVerify · PandaDoc · Phaxio · Telnyx · Google Workspace · WordPress</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Production Reliability</h2>
          <p>Integration Troubleshooting · Root-Cause Analysis · Logging · Exception Handling · Data Quality · Deduplication · Documentation · SOPs</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>AI and Developer Tools</h2>
          <p>OpenAI API · AI-Assisted Document Processing · GitHub · Playwright · BeautifulSoup · Astro · Local AI Workflows</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section container">
      <p class="section-label">How I work</p>
      <h2>Start with how the business really operates.</h2>
      <p>
        A reliable implementation starts with understanding people, processes,
        exceptions and the systems already in place. I work across technical
        and nontechnical teams to find an approach that will solve the problem
        without creating another one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Just as important is what happens after launch: tracing failures,
        improving usability, documenting decisions and leaving a system that
        other people can maintain.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="section container contact-section">
      <p class="section-label">Let's connect</p>
      <h2>Looking for someone who can connect the technical and business sides?</h2>
      <p>
        I'm interested in remote opportunities involving business systems
        engineering, technical implementation, automation, SaaS integrations,
        solutions engineering and customer-facing technical work.
      </p>
      <div class="contact-links">
        <a class="primary-link" href="mailto:aaronholmesdev@gmail.com">Email me</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/aaronholmesdev/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">LinkedIn profile</a>
        <a href="/resume">View résumé</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: 5rem 4.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-label,
  .project-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
  }

  .hero-links,
  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-link {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .section {
    width: min(calc(100% - 2rem), var(--content-width));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section > h2,
  .role-header h2,
  .project-card h2,
  .skills-grid h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .section > h2 {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
  }

  .section > p:not(.section-label) {
    max-width: var(--reading-width);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .role-block + .role-block {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .role-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .role-header h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
  }

  .role-company,
  .role-meta {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .role-summary {
    max-width: 820px;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  .experience-list {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .experience-list li + li {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .project-grid,
  .skills-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .project-card,
  .skills-grid > div {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.85rem;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .project-card h2,
  .skills-grid h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }

  .project-card p,
  .skills-grid p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .project-tech {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .additional-work {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  .additional-work h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  .additional-work p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .building-card {
    border-style: dashed !important;
  }

  .contact-section {
    padding-bottom: 6rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 800px) {
    .project-grid,
    .skills-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero {
      padding-block: 3.5rem;
    }

    .role-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .section {
      padding-block: 3rem;
    }

    .role-block + .role-block {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding-top: 3rem;
    }
  }

  .hero-note {
    max-width: 790px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .section-intro {
    max-width: var(--reading-width);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.07rem;
  }

  .role-block:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
  }

  .role-summary {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .project-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .project-card .project-tech {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .contact-links a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .contact-links a:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .contact-links .primary-link {
    color: var(--background);
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .project-card, .skills-grid > div { padding: 1.2rem; }
    .experience-list { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  }
</style>
